bpmn:name
    a                  owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    skos:prefLabel     "name"@en ;
    skos:definition    "The name of a BPMN element."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote     '''Faithful record of the BPMN XML `name` attribute: a plain xsd:string,
single-valued, with no language tag. This is a serialization-level property, not the canonical
Linked.Archi label.

skos:prefLabel is the canonical label. Every Linked.Archi consumer — documentation generators,
palette builders, deliverable templates, SPARQL reporting, SHACL validation — reads
skos:prefLabel and does not read bpmn:name. A graph that carries only bpmn:name is valid BPMN
but is not yet in Linked.Archi canonical form.

The two are not redundant. Of the 33 classes that carry a bpmn:name constraint, only 6 are
aligned to arch:Element (Collaboration, ConversationNode, DataStore, Lane, Message,
Participant). For the other 27 — Error, Signal, Interface, Operation, Resource, PartnerEntity,
PartnerRole, CorrelationKey, InputSet, OutputSet, DataInput, DataOutput, DataState, LaneSet,
Property, Category, MessageFlow, ConversationLink and the rest — bpmn:name is the only
name-bearing property, and no label shape applies to them because they are not architecture
elements.'''@en ;
    skos:editorialNote '''CONVERTER CONTRACT — emit both.

  1. skos:prefLabel — REQUIRED, and MUST carry a language tag. Mirror the BPMN name here for
     every class bpmnsh:RequiredNameShape targets (linkedarchi-bpmn-shacl.ttl). An untagged
     xsd:string literal does NOT satisfy it — the shape requires rdf:langString. Use the
     document language where the source declares one, "en" otherwise.
  2. bpmn:name — SHOULD be retained, unchanged, for round-trip fidelity and for the 27
     non-element classes above.

  ex:t1 a bpmn:ServiceTask ;
      bpmn:name      "Charge card" ;        # source attribute, verbatim
      skos:prefLabel "Charge card"@en .     # canonical label, language-tagged

Emitting bpmn:name alone leaves every element that must be named failing
bpmnsh:RequiredNameShape. Emitting skos:prefLabel alone validates cleanly but loses the
verbatim source attribute.

Note that not every arch:Element must be named: BPMN has 49 arch:Element classes and
bpmnsh:RequiredNameShape requires a label on 33 of them. Gateway and Event subtypes are
elements whose name BPMN leaves optional, so no label is required for them.

Deliberately NOT declared rdfs:subPropertyOf skos:prefLabel. That axiom looks like it would
bridge the two, but it does not: the entailed prefLabel inherits the plain xsd:string
datatype, so a correctly named element still fails — the failure merely moves from
sh:MinCountConstraintComponent to sh:DatatypeConstraintComponent, with a message that no
longer points at the real problem. The relationship between the two properties is policy,
stated here, not an inference.'''@en ;
.

